recast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Louisiana has consistently backed Republican presidential candidates by wide margins, and its partisan lean of roughly eleven points Republican sets the starting point for an open race in which neither party has a nominee. No candidate-level polling, expert ratings, or fundraising figures exist yet for the general election, so the forecast rests on the state's fundamentals.\n\nEarly 2028 activity is already visible: both parties' primaries are drawing attention, Senator John Kennedy has floated a run, and Kamala Harris has engaged in a redistricting fight touching Louisiana. None of this alters the structural picture. The Republican nominee starts with a clear advantage, and a Democratic win would require a substantial national shift. The rating is Likely Republican, with unusually wide uncertainty given how early and data-sparse the race remains.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.108, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.162, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.1608, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1621, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.1551, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.153, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.155, "margin": -11.0}]}